cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Nimbus in research, teaching or reporting, please cite it as
  below. Every simulation report the application prints names the commit
  that produced it and links to the validation report for that commit;
  cite that commit, or the release that contains it.
type: software
title: 'Nimbus — Nuclear & Impact Modeling & Blast Understanding System'
abstract: >-
  A browser-based simulator of asteroid impacts, nuclear and conventional
  explosions, earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, submarine landslides and the
  tsunamis they cause, with estimated casualties. Every quantity is traced
  to a published source; every death toll carries a 5–95 % predictive band
  drawn from the published scatter of its inputs; and the model is checked
  against recorded events — death tolls, buoy and survey wave heights, USGS
  ShakeMap footprints — in a validation report that continuous integration
  regenerates from the code and refuses to let drift from it.
authors:
  - given-names: Andrea
    family-names: Rossi
  - name: Nimbus contributors
repository-code: 'https://github.com/BayranLabSoftware/nimbus'
url: 'https://bayranlabsoftware.github.io/nimbus/'
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - natural hazards
  - tsunami
  - earthquake
  - asteroid impact
  - nuclear explosion effects
  - volcanic hazard
  - casualty estimation
  - uncertainty quantification
  - model validation
  - science communication
